st-hero\" data-load-strategy=\"exclude\">\n                    <figure data-type=\"img\" data-e2e-name=\"image-figure-image\" data-media-container=\"image\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/ImageObject\">\n                        <div>\n                          <meta itemprop=\"contentUrl\" content=\"https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=1200\">\n                          <p><img src=\"https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=700\" srcset=\"https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=400&format=jpeg&auto=webp 400w, https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=500&format=jpeg&auto=webp 500w, https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=700&format=jpeg&auto=webp 700w, https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=1000&format=jpeg&auto=webp 1000w, https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=1300&format=jpeg&auto=webp 1300w, https://i.insider.com/6afb67d9f0664acecacb9654?width=2000&format=jpeg&auto=webp 2000w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1280px) 900px\" alt=\"California Attorney General Rob Bonta\" decoding=\"sync\">\n                        </p></div>\n                    \n                          <figcaption data-e2e-name=\"image-caption\">Christina House / Los Angeles Times via Getty Images California Attorney General Rob Bonta</figcaption>\n                    </figure>\n              </div>\n    \n    \n    \n          \n    \n            <div data-e2e-name=\"post-details\">\n                \n                \n                \n                \n                  <p><time data-timestamp=\"2026-11-16T20:32:17.720Z\" data-disable-relative-formatting=\"\">\n                      2026-11-16T20:32:17.720Z\n                    </time>\n                  </p>\n              </div>\n    \n    \n          \n    \n            \n            \n            \n    \n          \n    \n      <section data-load-strategy=\"lazy\" data-component-type=\"image-modal\" data-track-content=\"\" data-post-type=\"story\" data-track-marfeel=\"post-body-content\">\n                \n                      <p>California Attorney General Rob Bonta is suing OpenAI over the cyberattack a group of its rogue models launched against the AI platform Hugging Face in July.</p><p>The lawsuit, filed in San Francisco Superior Court on Monday, alleges that OpenAI, one of the world's leading AI developers, endangered the public by testing its advanced models without having adequate safeguards in place. The suit asserts that the incident was foreseeable and preventable, and that OpenAI misled the public about the safety of its experiments.</p><p>\"OpenAI's actions escalated real-word cybersecurity risks, threatening the safety, health, and well-being of society,\" Bonta said in a statement. He added, \"In California, we value innovation, but we demand innovation that follows the law — no matter the product or the company.\"</p><p>The hack, Bonta said, \"was the predictable result of an internal culture at OpenAI that prioritizes growth and rapid model development over safety and accountability.\"</p><p>本文最初发表在 POLITICO 上，由阿克塞尔·施普林格全球记者网络提供，该网络利用公司新闻编辑室的资源来发布雄心勃勃的独家新闻、调查、采访、观点文章和分析。 它允许记者（包括来自 POLITICO、Business Insider、WELT、BILD、Onet 和 Fakt 的记者）跨平台合作为数亿国际受众撰写重大报道。</p>\n                \n                \n                  </section>\n    \n    \n    \n    \n      </section>\n\n    \n    <!-- Included desktop \"post-aside\" -->    \n\n    \n      \n      <section data-component-type=\"post-bottom\" data-load-strategy=\"exclude\" data-track-marfeel=\"post-bottom\">\n        <section>\n    \n    \n            \n            \n    \n            \n            \n            <section data-component-type=\"read-next\" data-e2e-name=\"read-next\" data-display-size=\"4\" data-post-id=\"6afb65b5bd239b74a94efa81\" data-root-margin=\"250px 0px\" data-track-view=\"{&quot;subscription_experience&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&q